{"name":"Alien Abduction","hex":"#0cff0c","fetched":"2026-10-20","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"alien abduction","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The abduction of a person by extraterrestrials."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/alien_abduction"}],"entries":[{"title":"Alien abduction","blocks":[{"text":"Alien abduction is the phenomenon claimed by people reporting that they or their patients have been kidnapped by extraterrestrial beings and subjected to physical and/or psychological experimentation. Most scientists and mental health professionals explain these experiences by factors such as suggestibility, sleep paralysis, deception, and psychopathology. Skeptic Robert Sheaffer sees similarity between some of the aliens described by abductees and those depicted in science fiction films, in particular Invaders From Mars (1953)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Walton%28reconstitution%29.png/330px-Walton%28reconstitution%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alien_abduction","wikidata":"Q892757"},{"title":"Alien Abduction (2014 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Alien Abduction is a 2014 American found-footage science fiction horror film and the directorial debut of Matty Beckerman. The movie was released to VOD on April 4, 2014, and also had a limited theatrical run. The film stars Riley Polanski as an autistic 11-year-old boy who records his ordeal as an alien abductee."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/5c/Alien_Abduction_2014_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alien_Abduction_(2014_film)","wikidata":"Q16960967"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Walton%28reconstitution%29.png/500px-Walton%28reconstitution%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbna